<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tejeros Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1897</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tejeros Convention was a meeting of Filipino revolutionaries held at Tejeros in Cavite on 22 March 1897 to settle the rivalry between the Magdalo and Magdiwang factions of the Katipunan. It elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> president of a revolutionary government in place of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-bonifacio">Andrés Bonifacio</a>, who rejected the result. Bonifacio was arrested and executed in May 1897.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tejeros-convention.jpg" alt="Tejeros Convention" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elmer B. Domingo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Casa_Hacienda,_Tejero,_Cavite.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
